REGULAR EXPRESSION MATCHING

(DP + Pattern Logic – Very Hard)

🔹 Problem Statement

Given:

String s

Pattern p

Implement regex matching with support for:

. → matches any single character

* → matches zero or more of the previous element

Return whether s matches p.

🔹 Example 1
s = "aa"
p = "a*"

Output:

true
🔹 Example 2
s = "ab"
p = ".*"

Output:

true
🔹 Example 3
s = "mississippi"
p = "mis*is*p*."

Output:

false
❗ Why This Is Hard

You must handle:

Character matching

Dot behavior

Star meaning:

zero occurrence

one occurrence

multiple occurrence

Greedy fails.
Simple recursion fails (exponential).

We need 2D DP.

🔥 Key Idea

Let:

dp[i][j] = 
Does first i characters of s 
match first j characters of p?
🔹 Base Case
dp[0][0] = true

Empty string matches empty pattern.

🔹 Character Match Rule

If:

s[i-1] == p[j-1]
OR
p[j-1] == '.'

Then:

dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j-1]
🔥 STAR CASE (Important)

If:

p[j-1] == '*'

Then we have 2 choices:

1️⃣ Treat star as ZERO occurrence

Ignore previous char + '*'

dp[i][j] = dp[i][j-2]
2️⃣ Treat star as ONE or MORE

If previous char matches current character:

p[j-2] == s[i-1]
OR
p[j-2] == '.'

Then:

dp[i][j] |= dp[i-1][j]

Why?

Because we consume one character from string,
but keep pattern same (since * can repeat).

🔥 Complete Transition
if p[j-1] != '*':
    if char matches:
        dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j-1]

else:
    dp[i][j] = dp[i][j-2]

    if previous char matches:
        dp[i][j] |= dp[i-1][j]
🔹 Java Code
class RegexMatching {

    public boolean isMatch(String s, String p) {

        int m = s.length();
        int n = p.length();

        boolean[][] dp = new boolean[m + 1][n + 1];

        dp[0][0] = true;

        // Handle patterns like a*, a*b*, a*b*c*
        for (int j = 2; j <= n; j++) {
            if (p.charAt(j - 1) == '*') {
                dp[0][j] = dp[0][j - 2];
            }
        }

        for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++) {
            for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {

                if (p.charAt(j - 1) != '*') {

                    if (p.charAt(j - 1) == s.charAt(i - 1) 
                        || p.charAt(j - 1) == '.') {

                        dp[i][j] = dp[i - 1][j - 1];
                    }

                } else {

                    // zero occurrence
                    dp[i][j] = dp[i][j - 2];

                    // one or more occurrence
                    if (p.charAt(j - 2) == s.charAt(i - 1) 
                        || p.charAt(j - 2) == '.') {

                        dp[i][j] |= dp[i - 1][j];
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        return dp[m][n];
    }
}
🔹 Time Complexity
O(m × n)
🔹 Space Complexity
O(m × n)
